From: Mihawk <163614687+mihawk-99@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 21:30:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: a FreeBSD machine without a battery is on mains power

fill_battery_state starts from zeros and sets AcOnLine only when the hw.acpi.battery sysctls exist, so a machine
without a battery (a desktop, the PS5) reported BatteryPresent FALSE and AcOnLine FALSE: GetSystemPowerStatus
answered ACLineStatus 0, "offline", which kernel32's power test notices and a game that throttles itself on battery
power would act on. Windows reports AC online for a machine with no battery, and so does this now.
---
  dlls/ntdll/unix/system.c | 5 +++++
  1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/system.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/system.c
index a944ded..15dfa2b 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/system.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/system.c
@@ -4927,6 +4927,11 @@ static NTSTATUS fill_battery_state( SYSTEM_BATTERY_STATE *bs )
             bs->MaxCapacity = 100;
         }
     }
+    else
+    {
+        /* no battery (a desktop, a console): the machine is on mains power, as Windows reports it */
+        bs->AcOnLine = TRUE;
+    }
     return STATUS_SUCCESS;
 }
 
